    "fullSolution": "**Find inverse of $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}$**\n\n**Step 1: Check invertibility**\n$$\\det(A) = (3)(2) - (1)(5) = 6 - 5 = 1 \\neq 0$$\nMatrix is invertible!\n\n**Step 2: Apply formula**\n$$A^{-1} = \\frac{1}{\\det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix} d & -b \\\\ -c & a \\end{bmatrix} = \\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}$$\n\n**Step 3: Verify**\n$$AA^{-1} = \\begin{bmatrix} 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix} = I$$\n\n**Answer:** $A^{-1} = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}$",
